-- title:
--   Eigenvalue splitting of Lie Y over a p-nilpotent base
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an element $\omega$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2} = W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})$ (`Zp2 p`), together with integers $t, n$ such that $x^2 - tx + n$ has no root in $\mathbb{Z}/p$, such that $\omega^2 = t\omega - n$, such that the Witt-vector Frobenius sends $\omega$ to $t - \omega$, and such that $\mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z}\omega$ is dense, in the sense that for every $k$ and every $x \in \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ there are integers $c, d$ with $x - (c + d\omega)$ in the ideal generated by $p^k$. Let $S$ be a commutative ring in which the image of $p$ is nilpotent, let $j : \mathbb{Z}_{p^2} \to S$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $Y$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $S$: a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $S$ equipped with an action `act` of $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ by endomorphisms of $F$ (multiplicative, additive, with `act 1` the identity) and a uniformiser series `varpi`, an endomorphism of $F$ with `varpi ∘ varpi = act p` and `varpi ∘ act a = act (Frobenius a) ∘ varpi`. Write $T =$ [`MvFormalGroup.linearPart (Y.act ω)`](def/MvFormalGroup_BasicV2.html#L359) for the $2 \times 2$ matrix of linear coefficients of the action of $\omega$ on $Y$, and $a = j\omega$, $b = j(\text{Frobenius }\omega)$. The conclusion is a conjunction of five assertions: $a - b$ is a unit in $S$; $(T - a \cdot 1)(T - b \cdot 1) = 0$ in $M_2(S)$; the submodule `Y.lieZero j`, defined as the intersection over all $c \in \mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ of the kernels of $\mathrm{linearPart}(Y.\mathrm{act}\,c) - j(c)$ acting on $Y.\mathrm{Lie}$ by matrix multiplication, equals the kernel of $T - a \cdot 1$; the submodule `Y.lieOne j`, defined as the intersection over all $c$ of the kernels of $\mathrm{linearPart}(Y.\mathrm{act}\,c) - j(\text{Frobenius }c)$, equals the kernel of $T - b \cdot 1$; and these two submodules are complementary in $Y.\mathrm{Lie}$.
--
--   This is the splitting of the Lie module of a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over a base in which $p$ is nilpotent into the two eigenspaces for the unramified subring $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$, the two eigencharacters being $j$ and $j \circ \mathrm{Frobenius}$; the discriminant $t^2 - 4n$ of the quadratic satisfied by $\omega$ is invertible, which makes the two eigenspaces complementary and cut out by the single element $\omega$. It supports the criterion [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_idempotent_isSpecial_map_iff`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_idempotent_isSpecial_map_iff) in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development, where speciality of a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module is expressed through idempotents splitting the Lie module.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_isCompl_lieZero_lieOne_and_eq_ker_of_isNilpotent.lean

